; Ceiling fan globe. Grouped "ceiling_light", so QualityManager overwrites the
; energy to 0.8 desktop / 0.6 Quest — the authored value here is only what shows
; before it runs.
;
; It sits at y 2.29, the centre of the glass globe (which spans 2.227..2.357),
; and casts NO shadow. At 2.35 it was up against the motor housing and, with
; shadows on, the shade boxed it in completely: the fan lit nothing at all.
; Frosted glass is translucent and Godot's shadow map is not, so the shade has to
; be taken out of the equation rather than worked around. It opts out via the
; "no_shadow" group, not a shadow_enabled property: QualityManager.configure_light
; writes shadow_enabled on every Light3D in the tree, so an authored false here
; was silently overwritten every run. Shadows are off on
; Quest anyway, so this also makes the desktop view match the headset.
;
; The cull mask is the price of that: with no shadow to stop it, a 7 m light
; would reach straight through the walls and into the suburb outside, so it is
; masked to layer 1 the way Dusk already is.
[node name="FanGlobeLight" type="OmniLight3D" parent="." groups=["ceiling_light", "no_shadow"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 2.29, 0)
light_color = Color(1, 0.85, 0.62, 1)
light_energy = 1.2
light_cull_mask = 1
omni_range = 7.0

; Carpet bounce. A real floor throws light back up into the underside of the bed,
; the desk and the sills, and with no GI and no shadows there is nothing else in
; this room doing that — which is why furniture undersides read as painted-on.
;
; Deliberately WIDE and DIM rather than small and bright: a tiny near-surface
; light dies on the mobile backend, rendering as black, a flat disc or garbage.
; Sits at 1.1 m with a nearly flat falloff. It was first authored at 0.35 m and
; energy 0.35, which put a visible POOL of light on the carpet in the middle of
; the room — an omni that low is close enough to the floor to relight it as a
; source rather than stand in for its bounce. High, dim and flat is what reads
; as bounce; low and bright reads as a lamp lying on the carpet.
; Parented to FanGlobeLight, and that is load-bearing rather than tidiness. As a
; sibling it was an always-on light nothing could switch off: with every
; switchable light off at night it MORE THAN DOUBLED the room, mean frame luma
; 0.256 against 0.115 without it. It is meant to be the ceiling light's bounce,
; so it has to die with the ceiling light — and light_switch.gd toggles
; `visible` on that fixture, which hides its children too. Deliberately NOT in
; the "ceiling_light" group: QualityManager._adjust_lights rewrites the energy
; of everything in that group, which would turn this into a second ceiling
; globe. Local Y is -1.19 to sit at 1.1 m world.
; Masked to layer 1 and no_shadow like every other interior light, or it would
; reach out into the suburb.
[node name="FloorBounce" type="OmniLight3D" parent="FanGlobeLight" groups=["no_shadow"]]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -1.19, 0)
light_color = Color(1, 0.88, 0.74, 1)
light_energy = 0.18
light_cull_mask = 1
omni_range = 8.0
omni_attenuation = 0.35

; Golden-hour sun through the window. It is a SpotLight3D rather than a
; DirectionalLight because shadows are off on QUEST, so a directional sun there
; lights the room through its walls. The cone does the occluding a shadow map
; would normally do — at the window plane it is 1.27 m
; across against a 1.5 x 1.2 m opening, so nothing spills onto the wall around it.
;
; Energy is owned by the blinds, which scale it by how far they are open. The
; authored 3.0 is what shows with them fully raised.
; NOT in "no_shadow", unlike every other light in this room, and that is what
; puts blind-slat shadows across the floor. QualityManager.configure_light gives
; any light outside that group `shadows_enabled()`, which is true on the desktop
; MEDIUM preset and false on the Quest LOW one — so the slat shadows are a PCVR
; feature that costs the headset nothing and needs no code to switch. The cone
; still does the occluding on Quest exactly as it did before.
[node name="WindowSun" type="SpotLight3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(-0.991, -0.057, 0.116, 0, 0.895, 0.444, -0.129, 0.44, -0.888, -0.6, 2.6, -4.5)
light_color = Color(1, 0.83, 0.62, 1)
light_energy = 3.6
light_cull_mask = 1
spot_range = 12.0
spot_angle = 11.0
spot_angle_attenuation = 0.55
